# teslamate-rs statically links 169 Debian crates (axum, reqwest, rustls,
# tokio and their trees), so the generated Static-Built-Using runs just over
# lintian's 5000-character limit. The field is generated by
# dh-cargo-built-using and is the accurate provenance record Policy asks for
# when static linking; truncating it would lose security-tracking data.
# Larger Rust binaries in the archive ship longer fields still (sccache is
# over 7000 characters), so this is not an ftp-master blocker.
teslamate-rs: field-too-long Static-Built-Using (* chars > *)
